Root Cause:-  1) Access control was implemented only at the front-end (proxy/filter layer).
          
              2) The backend trusted the X-Original-URL header supplied by the client.
          
              3) The backend did not perform proper authorization checks for sensitive endpoints.

Vulnerability Type:- URL-based access control bypass
